  "request_text": "## TND-A-B02: analytical consequence or representation-only disposition\n\nAsk what becomes more accessible about the original H through the assessed model. Select at most one target: a usable finite-order identity, quantitative estimate, conditioning bound, or source-sensitive restriction with its exact domain and scale. Compare with direct analysis using the same source information. A representation alone is a valid physical result but supplies no estimating advantage automatically.\n\nApply the control screen in the [overview][overview] to the proposed premises and witness domains. State whether the target is an intermediate estimate, diagnostic, physical interpretation or target-equivalent reformulation. Keep the inherited heat/linear benchmark and other failures within their proved classes.\n\n**Output/completion:** one decision and, only if a method is fixed, one bounded E03 request; otherwise a representation-only stop or one missing estimate. **Limit:** one target, at most two analytical approaches to it, one decision pass. No new physical mechanism here: return to B01 for that. No numerical plan is activated.\n\n",
